<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:23:40Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Indonesia: Second ferry disaster in five days</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5b19f8b8af8f16a8b50d5b664cf3492c9827b3d42acc9ad621a40a35852fe418</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:22:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T13:17:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/indonesia-second-ferry-disaster-in-five-days--bcdea8ab2589.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/indonesia-second-ferry-disaster-in-five-days" /><summary type="html">At least one person has died and more than 100 people remain missing after a ferry carrying 243 people sank in rough weather between the Indonesian islands of Java and Borneo. The disaster is the second major ferry accident in the region in five days, renewing concerns over safety standards, overcrowding and maintenance.</summary></entry><entry><title>Yemen: Fighting escalates around the Bab el-Mandeb Strait</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ff24e1dc829daea5d95a48aea186519b46cda5e5ff5d009cf469d046dd1e09a</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:22:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T13:15:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/yemen-fighting-escalates-around-the-bab-el-mandeb-strait--7a2aac2b3186.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/yemen-fighting-escalates-around-the-bab-el-mandeb-strait" /><summary type="html">Fighting is escalating in Yemen after Iran-backed Houthi forces seized strategic territory around the Bab el-Mandeb Strait, prompting counterstrikes by government forces and reported Saudi air raids. The Houthis also claimed attacks inside southern Saudi Arabia and threatened to disrupt shipping through the key maritime chokepoint, raising fears for regional security and global trade.</summary></entry><entry><title>Swedish far-right eyes role in government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c6f833a2095ad4b52765869c975d17d0f451c19fb464a381fe9bc18f238742a6</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:22:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T13:11:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/swedish-far-right-eyes-role-in-government--89cf8fdd015f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/swedish-far-right-eyes-role-in-government" /><summary type="html">As Sweden heads into a closely fought election, the far right is gaining ground by tapping into concerns over crime and security, issues that some voters increasingly associate with migration. On FRANCE 24, Stockholm University sociologist Zeth Isaksson said the movement has also softened its image in recent years, making it more acceptable to a broader electorate, while also cautioning against overstating the strength of the far right in Sweden.</summary></entry><entry><title>Radio France staff strike over appointment of far-right weekly editor</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c773c5c820e0b66f7cc05608b92abba0f7a471be12ec286e2b3cc1dbb2260a8f</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:22:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T12:44:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20260913-radio-france-staff-strike-over-appointment-of-far-right-weekly-editor--07059883adf7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260913-radio-france-staff-strike-over-appointment-of-far-right-weekly-editor" /><summary type="html">Staff at public broadcaster Radio France began a two-day strike on Sunday over the appointment of Charles Sapin, deputy editor-in-chief at far-right weekly Valeurs Actuelles. Unions accuse Sapin of promoting far-right ideas ahead of next spring's presidential election, while management has defended the appointment in the name of pluralism.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil: Michelle Bolsonaro's key role in the presidential race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a0d12e1f1f464ca0c7545704a91c18d777b892a41b8180838dd5dbe640f824bb</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:22:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T11:08:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/brazil-michelle-bolsonaro-s-key-role-in-the-presidential-race--c6d331e45ad7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-michelle-bolsonaro-s-key-role-in-the-presidential-race" /><summary type="html">Brazil is heading to the polls on October 4, with President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva seeking a fourth term as the Bolsonaro family mounts a political comeback through Flávio's presidential bid and Michelle's Senate campaign. With polls pointing to another tight race, Michelle's popularity among women could prove crucial as the family tries to return to power.</summary></entry><entry><title>The week in pictures: 9/11 anniversary, far-right win in Germany and Houthis' Yemen offensive</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4258174492f443055773c92874eecd1d104423531bb5b66fb7963e42c689b77a</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:22:47Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T10:48:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260913-the-week-in-pictures-9-11-anniversary-far-right-win-germany-houthis-yemen-offensive--652ff4e85a45.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260913-the-week-in-pictures-9-11-anniversary-far-right-win-germany-houthis-yemen-offensive" /><summary type="html">A look back at some of the week's key news stories and the most striking images, from commemorations marking 25 years since the 9/11 attacks to the breakthrough win for Germany's far-right AfD party and the lightening offensive that has left Yemen's Iran-backed Houthi rebels in control of the country's Red Sea coast.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Sweden election: A turning point for the far right?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8720261729347ff113adc54b0b3c63572f41a0050eeaf75141ef8cdabb701c90</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:22:50Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T09:48:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sweden-election-a-turning-point-for-the-far-right--20fbe48330d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sweden-election-a-turning-point-for-the-far-right" /><summary type="html">The stakes are high in Sweden's general election, with the far right poised to enter government for the first time. TV4 News journalist Markus Karlsson-Bourrioux explains how opinion polls shifted from a comfortable centre-left lead to a tight race over the summer, and how far-right ideas have gained ground since the last election in 2022.</summary></entry><entry><title>Germany: Thousands rally against far-right after AfD victory</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4a5be92b03592d6f497080773c193db331d6047f9a59a8998c3230f58972f690</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:22:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T09:41:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/germany-thousands-rally-against-far-right-after-afd-victory--38396b69fe17.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/germany-thousands-rally-against-far-right-after-afd-victory" /><summary type="html">Tens of thousands of people marched in around 20 cities across Germany to protest the rise of the far right after the AfD's historic victory in the Saxony-Anhalt state election. Demonstrators said they were defending democracy as mainstream parties continue to rule out governing with the AfD.</summary></entry><entry><title>BRICS summit: What came out of the New Delhi meeting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3cc4102651506479c59f87e97262968b17b16c4302497638f2653bf69edd802b</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:22:55Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T09:27:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/brics-summit-what-came-out-of-the-new-delhi-meeting--2d7ab6cb6280.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/brics-summit-what-came-out-of-the-new-delhi-meeting" /><summary type="html">The BRICS summit in New Delhi ended with a joint declaration calling for greater Global South influence in global governance and urging restraint in the Middle East. The gathering also served as a platform for one-to-one diplomacy, with leaders holding a series of bilateral meetings aimed at easing regional tensions. FRANCE 24's Navodita Kumari has the details.</summary></entry><entry><title>UK: Police probe £72 million donation to Reform UK</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3cd9df9eef5d4ec7f09dc2012f1ca6ba1f6211988caef49ef988f37a9bd06eb2</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:22:58Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T09:26:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260913-uk-police-probe-_72-million-donation-to-reform-uk--7eb204a7eff8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260913-uk-police-probe-%C2%A372-million-donation-to-reform-uk" /><summary type="html">British police have opened a criminal investigation into a £72 million donation to Nigel Farage's Reform UK, amid questions over whether the funds breached rules on foreign political donations. The probe comes as anti-immigration protests and counter-demonstrations intensify across England, highlighting growing tensions over immigration and national identity.</summary></entry><entry><title>Macron, Carney to visit North Atlantic French islands after Trump's map post</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e0f60915ec802880af384351d8a7271bdbc52f65b204583667b85478c47fc543</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:23:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T09:25:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260913-macron-carney-to-visit-french-islands-after-trump-s-map-post--f17f71093187.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260913-macron-carney-to-visit-french-islands-after-trump-s-map-post" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron and Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney will reaffirm the “sovereignty of nations” on a visit on September 20 to Saint-Pierre-et-Miquelon, a French territory in the North Atlantic, the Élysée Palace announced on Sunday. The symbolic trip comes after US President Donald Trump posted a map on social media showing the entire North American continent covered by the US flag.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen: Houthi offensive triggers new displacement crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ef053cddf148d32e3d984cd326f36243a95aec7df65dc80056c62db9d489856a</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:23:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T09:18:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/yemen-houthi-offensive-triggers-new-displacement-crisis--2ca71fdc0d39.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/yemen-houthi-offensive-triggers-new-displacement-crisis" /><summary type="html">More than 70,000 people have fled their homes in Yemen after Iran-backed Houthi rebels launched an offensive to seize the Bab el-Mandeb Strait, with many escaping to Aden and around 1,400 crossing into neighbouring Djibouti. The UN and IOM warn the new displacement wave is worsening an already dire humanitarian crisis in a country devastated by 12 years of war.</summary></entry><entry><title>France apologises for diplomatic spat with US to lift block on new ambassador to Washington</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:efe00f3abcbd37c9d39aa9ebf3df57d695b63d1f2f8099b699efd6818cdbe1f7</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:23:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T09:01:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20260913-france-apologises-for-diplomatic-spat-with-us-to-lift-block-on-new-ambassador-to-washington--6f9350753c15.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260913-france-apologises-for-diplomatic-spat-with-us-to-lift-block-on-new-ambassador-to-washington" /><summary type="html">The French UN mission said it regretted an online post criticising a US vote at the UN General Assembly in a move that should clear the way for the new French ambassador Aurélien Lechevallier to take up his post in Washington.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>On Sept 12th, 'everyone was compassionate': The world needs 'to be together again' - Richard Roeill</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e4528fd4975498a477216b45a7a55c078463d64284dfbc0678033d0e88f3ca38</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:23:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T07:18:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260913-on-sept-12th-everyone-was-compassionate-the-world-needs-to-be-together-again-richard-roeill--bad1381d87fa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260913-on-sept-12th-everyone-was-compassionate-the-world-needs-to-be-together-again-richard-roeill" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Richard Roeill, former New York Firefighter and 9/11 First Responder. His testimony reframes the legacy of September 11th not as a historical event confined to a single day, but as living history. The former New York City firefighter describes an anniversary that reactivates trauma, while the illnesses suffered by first responders make the consequences of Ground Zero ever present decades later. Yet Roeill’s testimony is not simply a narrative of sacrifice. He says that responders were misled about the dangers they faced, demanding accountability and long-term healthcare for those exposed to the very toxic air.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Olympic rematch: US and France to meet for women's FIBA World Cup title</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:09179304551f0f6eb443d9a0f01b662c80c7d31f270e0e1d39dceefdbcf0a2e9</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:23:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T06:48:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sport/20260913-olympic-rematch-us-and-france-to-meet-for-women-s-fiba-world-cup-title--4ae45ec08999.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20260913-olympic-rematch-us-and-france-to-meet-for-women-s-fiba-world-cup-title" /><summary type="html">France won against host Germany in the women's FIBA World Cup semifinals Saturday and will now face the United States in the final Sunday after the four-time defending champion and tournament favorite defeated Spain in the other semifinal.</summary><category term="Sport" /></entry><entry><title>Swedes vote in close general election that could usher far right into government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c36c5b143f27c462c6d0c2a6f0a59090bf70121bbbab1f409a6f4d91d7d14abb</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:23:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T06:16:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260913-swedes-vote-in-close-general-election-that-could-usher-far-right-into-government--c14a0b3c76df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260913-swedes-vote-in-close-general-election-that-could-usher-far-right-into-government" /><summary type="html">Swedes are heading to the polls Sunday for a general election that will either bring a far right party into government for the first time or shift the country back towards the liberalism it has long been known for. The centre-left opposition holds a narrow lead over the ruling right-wing bloc but Prime ⁠Minister Ulf Kristersson's four-party alliance – which includes the far right Sweden Democrats – has been catching up in the final weeks of campaigning.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Middle East live: Houthis say hit Saudi base after renewed fighting with Yemeni forces</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4a5be118bf0e5c71308f1727a09dee8fd75a5d996d9bf10203202b747b19385c</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:23:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T05:11:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260913-middle-east-live-houthis-say-hit-saudi-base-after-renewed-fighting-with-yemeni-forces--80232e475ad4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260913-middle-east-live-houthis-say-hit-saudi-base-after-renewed-fighting-with-yemeni-forces" /><summary type="html">Yemeni Houthi rebels claimed responsibility on Sunday for an attack on a military base in southern Saudi Arabia as renewed fighting with Yemen's government forces forced growing numbers of civilians to flee. Fighting in western Yemen over the past few weeks has left hundreds dead and displaced tens of thousands of people. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>'Second life': Nepal hydropower tunnel survivor recalls ordeal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f34de871ec87a24e17e9ae1c1d3be4cd919f81a74d6553a5cb89e9484adfca54</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:23:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T04:17:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260913-second-life-nepal-hydropower-tunnel-survivor-recalls-ordeal--bac6c1a764d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260913-second-life-nepal-hydropower-tunnel-survivor-recalls-ordeal" /><summary type="html">Nepali hydropower worker Sanjay Sah survived in total darkness inside a tunnel flooded by the deadly flash flood that struck the China-Nepal border on August 26, drinking muddy water and praying that rescuers would find him. The survivor, who was rescued on September 4, recalls the 10 days he spent stranded.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Saudi Arabia closes East-West pipeline as Houthis tighten grip on Red Sea</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3ae77c6a5b9b23817efa2df5975fe2bba617d67b9af611350d98ba8033021cca</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:23:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T20:51:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260912-saudi-arabia-shut-down-east-west-pipeline-as-houthis-tighten-grip-on-red-sea--806e159c0921.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260912-saudi-arabia-shut-down-east-west-pipeline-as-houthis-tighten-grip-on-red-sea" /><summary type="html">Saudi Arabia on Saturday ​shut down the vital East-West pipeline after the conduit came under attack in the widening Middle East war, threatening to send energy prices soaring. The 1,200-km pipeline has served as the main route out for global ​supplies of Middle East oil for the ‌past six months while the Strait of Hormuz has been largely shut by war.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Céline Dion makes historic Paris comeback, six years after last tour</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2fea62914857e6b56982619f8b2c924e53aa165bfd66edfb6795ea9924d4628e</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:23:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T20:05:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/culture/20260912-c_line-dion-makes-historic-comeback-in-paris-six-years-after-last-tour--6bb28623a8fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/culture/20260912-c%C3%A9line-dion-makes-historic-comeback-in-paris-six-years-after-last-tour" /><summary type="html">Beloved French Canadian singer Céline Dion on Saturday returned to the stage after years battling a rare neurological disorder with a sell-out concert in an arena west of Paris. The 58-year-old appeared visibly moved as she opened her first full concert in six years to a crowd of around 30,000 people.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Danish WWII drama wins Golden Lion at Venice Film Festival</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1fa48d5b8be67719003658bcce7be2271142e1c9fef51703f9ccff78c358ca86</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:23:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T19:15:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/culture/20260912-danish-wwii-drama-wins-golden-lion-at-venice-film-festival--0e1352043e95.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/culture/20260912-danish-wwii-drama-wins-golden-lion-at-venice-film-festival" /><summary type="html">A Danish WWII drama about a woman trying to hide a wartime relationship with a Nazi was awared top prize on Saturday at The Venice Film Festival, while Gaza documentary NAZA snagged the special jury prize. "Unknown Woman" had been a major talking point of the festival due to its subject matter, which has rarely been explored in film, and because director May el-Toukhy was almost alone as a woman director in the event.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Has Trump Left MBS hanging over Yemen?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8abfe5f46027157bf55e009733d7dffbb6e174635d98d6e098f729e68e37f323</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:23:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T18:49:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260912-has-trump-left-mbs-hanging-over-yemen--36647a88beb9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260912-has-trump-left-mbs-hanging-over-yemen" /><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Tens of thousands protest against far-right AfD party in Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:257c5b696799c831fc3c4948b4b20c6efff5ed7b471285cdbc00751c3d06af4d</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:23:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T17:12:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260912-tens-of-thousands-of-people-protest-in-germany-against-far-right-afd--3bb68df54c54.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260912-tens-of-thousands-of-people-protest-in-germany-against-far-right-afd" /><summary type="html">About 150,000 demonstrators took to the streets in around 20 cities across Germany on Saturday against the far-right AfD, after the party scored a crushing victory in a state election last week. The Alternative for Germany (AfD) topped the vote in the eastern region of Saxony-Anhalt, and is now seeking to form the first extreme-right state government in Germany since World War II.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>France beats Germany to reach first women's World Cup basketball final</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fbff9b961c0df423b4b3dc48b2e8390eb128214271282ab5f387692ab723ef6c</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:23:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T16:29:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sport/20260912-france-beats-germany-to-reach-first-women-s-world-cup-basketball-final--401011b73ca6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20260912-france-beats-germany-to-reach-first-women-s-world-cup-basketball-final" /><summary type="html">France beat Germany Saturday and made it through to the final of the women's basketball World Cup for the first time after a 86-64 victory. Gabby Williams top scored with 22 points for the Olympic silver medalists, who kept their unbeaten record at the tournament alive before Sunday's decider in Berlin.</summary><category term="Sport" /></entry></feed>
